# Prime review — 0515.prime-cycle 05.02

Date: 2026-10-30. Reviewer: Codex Prime.
Disposition: accepted for bounded current-Prime use of the experimental adapter.
No app wiring, kernel seating, canonical-state migration or fresh-Prime activation.

Prime independently ran 14 existing tests and 12 correction/journal tests: all 26
passed, no skips. Capture 0171 freshly verifies complete with eight payloads.
All 18 declared code, documentation, test and evidence files match hashes and lengths.
Builder reports additional mutation and Colab checks; Prime did not rerun those.

PC-01 is corrected: changed page/custody/direction and unusable review evidence stop
counting old declarations as current completion. The historical declaration and
next action remain visible. A hold remains blocking; freshness is not permission.
PC-02 is corrected: changed agreement.scope refuses the old template, with the
changed field named. The agreement, book and review location are bound; observation
timestamps and unrelated output placement are excluded. A successor needs a fresh
read. Legacy records retain their original meaning and are not upgraded silently.

The daily journal records actual adapter operations, with explicit coverage and
failure states. Tests cover replay without duplicate completion, interrupted
operations, start failure and logging failure after an already committed review.
The daily view separates declarations from current status and re-verifies reviews.
This is a useful connection between the review tools, not yet a complete desk.

Limits remain: local trusted-user operation; no same-user race safety or multi-file
transaction; no chat capture, dispatcher or model authentication. Link behaviour is
not independently exercised by these suites. AR-01 remains held and no affected
inventory/bridge fixtures were run. No model benchmark or usage saving is claimed.

One documentation clarification: DAILY-LOG says reasons are never copied into the
journal, but it also retains the exact decision.json input. That input includes
judgment and reasons. The work-local record remains authoritative; the input copy
is evidence, not a second decision authority. This wording does not block bounded
use, but should be clarified in a later documentation pass.

Next bounded action: current Prime should run one actual journalled read, supplied
review record, re-read and daily inspection against previously reviewed work.
Keep the page goal open where broader current-desk integration remains unfinished.
Do this before another cold-Prime Colab or more feature packs.

## First actual use completed

After acceptance, Codex Prime used the adapter on the already reviewed 0169 work.
The first read exposed the unmapped prose review; Prime explicitly adopted that
judgment, then a new process read returned reviewed/accepted, pass finished, goal
open. A separate daily view re-verified one unique review across three complete
logged operations. Exact input and output snapshots are preserved in actual-use/.
The source is pinned historical work, not a current desk queue or fresh-model test.
The next step is using this bounded route in routine reviews and observing manual
friction before adding more tools or claiming the complete work-pass loop is closed.
